      },
      "worked": "The definitions require $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$ and $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=\\frac{1-\\cos^2\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\\\a&=\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\\\b&=\\frac{1-\\sin^2\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}\\\\b&=\\frac{\\cos^2\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}\\\\a^2b^2&=\\frac{\\sin^4\\theta\\cos^4\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta\\sin^2\\theta}\\\\a^2b^2&=\\sin^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta\\end{align*}$$\n\nUsing $x^3+y^3=(x+y)^3-3xy(x+y)$,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin^6\\theta+\\cos^6\\theta&=(\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta)^3-3\\sin^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta(\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta)\\\\\\sin^6\\theta+\\cos^6\\theta&=1-3\\sin^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a^2b^2(a^2+b^2+3)&=\\sin^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta\\left(\\frac{\\sin^4\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta}+\\frac{\\cos^4\\theta}{\\sin^2\\theta}+3\\right)\\\\a^2b^2(a^2+b^2+3)&=\\sin^6\\theta+\\cos^6\\theta+3\\sin^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta\\\\a^2b^2(a^2+b^2+3)&=1-3\\sin^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta+3\\sin^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta\\\\a^2b^2(a^2+b^2+3)&=1\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
